 "why": "Kept for what it is by construction, with its small measured effect said plainly. All-star's opponents now have the human's legs exactly (speed_scale x red_skill = 1.0; 1.035 before). Their MEAN speed in play fell only from 1.07 to 1.06 of his (10.33 to 10.13 m/s against 9.55): the rest is not legs, it is that they sprint in every window their bar allows, under the same bar rule as the human since E05, and that is play. So T9 as I wrote it (mean speed within 5 %) measured the wrong thing; the level table reads it as \"top speed equal by rule\" from here. Wins did not move beyond the noise in five of six cells (planning hand 25 to 21.7 / 61.7 to 65.0 / 76.7 to 90.0, the last +13.3 +-6.9; thirdjam's 8.3 / 43.3 to 45 / 53.3); all-star stays far harder than pro for every hand.",
 "owner_line": "At all-star nobody out-skates you any more by having faster legs. They still hunt you from across the ice, lift your stick twice as often as pro does, and sprint whenever their bar lets them, as you can.",
 "notes": "Epoch k8-4. A level's number only (levels.all_star). The good planning hand's +13.3 is 1.9 standard errors in one cell of six: watch it in the 200-seed ladder."
}
